IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nzs-types`
IMPORT `nzs-entitlement`

-- New Zealand Superannuation and Retirement Income Act 2001 — GOAL 2:
-- ABSENCE AND PAYMENT OVERSEAS.
--
--   "Is New Zealand superannuation payable during this absence; and how
--    much is payable to someone living overseas or in a specified Pacific
--    country?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2001_84.txt — ss 21-35.

§ `Goal 2 — absence and payment overseas`

-- s 21 "A person is not entitled to New Zealand superannuation while that
-- person is absent from New Zealand except as provided in sections 22 to 35
-- ...". s 22 it "is payable in respect of the first 26 weeks of any absence
-- from New Zealand if— (a) the person's absence does not exceed 30 weeks; or
-- (b) the person's absence exceeds 30 weeks and the chief executive is
-- satisfied that the absence beyond 30 weeks is due to circumstances beyond
-- that person's control that he or she could not reasonably have foreseen
-- before departure."
@ref ss 21, 22
@export Whether New Zealand superannuation is payable for a week of a temporary absence under ss 21-22 of the New Zealand Superannuation and Retirement Income Act 2001: only within the first 26 weeks, and only if the whole absence is no more than 30 weeks or the time beyond 30 weeks is due to unforeseeable circumstances beyond the person's control. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN x IS AN `Absence facts`  @desc The week of the absence in question, the total length of the absence, and whether any time beyond 30 weeks was unforeseeable and beyond the person's control
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is payable during the temporary absence` x IF
        x's `weeks absent so far` AT MOST 26
    AND (    x's `total weeks absent` AT MOST 30
         OR  x's `absence beyond 30 weeks unforeseeable and beyond control`)

-- s 23: up to 2 years in total for medical treatment overseas with Ministry
-- of Health assistance; s 24: up to 156 weeks with a recognised aid agency.
@ref ss 23, 24
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER, medical IS A BOOLEAN, aid IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the chief executive may pay during an absence of` weeks `weeks, for medical treatment:` medical `, for aid work:` aid IF
        (medical AND weeks AT MOST 104)
    OR  (aid AND weeks AT MOST 156)

-- s 26A(1) "(a) treating each period during which the person ... has resided
-- in New Zealand while aged 20 or more and less than 65 as whole calendar
-- months and (where applicable) additional days; and (b) adding the number of
-- additional days (if any), dividing the total by 30, and disregarding any
-- remainder; and (c) adding the number of calendar months and the quotient
-- ...; and (d) dividing by 540 the total". FORK F2: the proportion is not
-- more than 1 (540 months is the 45 years from 20 to 65).
@ref ss 26(6), 26A
@export The proportion of the rate payable to a person living overseas under ss 26 and 26A of the New Zealand Superannuation and Retirement Income Act 2001: whole months of New Zealand residence between 20 and 65, plus the additional days divided by 30 (remainder disregarded), divided by 540. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN x IS AN `Absence facts`  @desc The whole calendar months and additional days of residence in New Zealand between ages 20 and 65
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the proportion payable overseas for` x MEANS
    min 1 ((x's `whole calendar months resident in New Zealand aged 20 to 65` PLUS FLOOR (x's `additional days resident in New Zealand aged 20 to 65` DIVIDED BY 30)) DIVIDED BY 540)

-- s 32 "(1)(a) ... a person who has resided in New Zealand for 20 or more
-- years since turning 20 years, the base rate: (b) ... for 10 or more years
-- but fewer than 20 years ..., an amount calculated using the following
-- formula" — symbols lost; read as base rate × years ÷ 20 (BRIEF.md).
-- Fewer than 10 years: s 32 gives no rate, so the encoding refuses (changed
-- after the independent pass; s 8(2)(a) would normally bar entitlement).
@ref ss 31, 32
@export The rate of New Zealand superannuation payable in a specified Pacific country under s 32 of the New Zealand Superannuation and Retirement Income Act 2001: the base rate for 20 or more years of New Zealand residence since 20; for 10 to 19 years, the base rate times the whole years divided by 20; no rate (refused) for fewer than 10. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN x IS AN `Absence facts`  @desc The whole years resident in New Zealand since turning 20
      base IS A NUMBER  @desc The base rate (the single sharing or couple rate in Schedule 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Pacific rate for` x `, base rate` base MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF years AT LEAST 20 THEN base
        IF years AT LEAST 10 THEN base TIMES years DIVIDED BY 20
        OTHERWISE `s 32 gives no rate for fewer than 10 years of residence in New Zealand since 20`
    WHERE
        years MEANS FLOOR (x's `whole years resident in New Zealand since 20`)

`s 32 gives no rate for fewer than 10 years of residence in New Zealand since 20` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 32 gives no rate for fewer than 10 years of residence in New Zealand since 20"

-- ss 29(2), 33(2): on death, payments overseas end on a date "not more than 4
-- weeks after the date of death".
@ref ss 29(2), 33(2)
GIVEN died IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day overseas payments may run to, died` died MEANS
    `the day` 28 `days after` died
